# Entry-form (not `deployment/artifacts/`) so the negation below takes effect; every
# subdirectory still matches as an entry, so calib-jetson/, features/, figures/,
# jetson-measurements/ and r48-parity-fixture/ stay ignored - they hold real worker
# frames, TRT engines and multi-MB logs. Only files named below are distributable.
deployment/artifacts/*
# Per-clip ensemble logits for the 64-clip test subset (12 KB, CC BY 4.0 with
# attribution to [5] in its header). It is the only artifact that makes Table 4.5
# independently checkable, and run_export_perclip_csv.py regenerates it.
!deployment/artifacts/per-clip-logits-test64.csv
# Device measurement records from the Jetson runs. These are the one class of artifact in this
# directory that is NOT reproducible from this repository: each carries `is_device_number: true`
# and re-creating it needs the board, so losing the file loses the measurement, whereas the worker
# frames, TRT engines and logs the rule above is aimed at are all rebuilt on the device. 91 earlier
# records are already tracked and the blanket entry was silently keeping the rest of the same
# series out. JSON only, ~32 KB each; the .mp4 fixture clips beside them stay ignored.
!deployment/artifacts/jetson-measurements/
deployment/artifacts/jetson-measurements/*
!deployment/artifacts/jetson-measurements/*.json
# Clean-window guard verdicts, one pair per run (thermal state, DVFS state, no competing process).
# They are what makes each measurement above interpretable rather than merely recorded. 1.9 KB each.
!deployment/artifacts/round3-device/
# Reference embeddings the device parity gate is checked against, written on the host from the FP32
# ONNX. Without them the FP16 verdicts in deployment/JETSON-RUNBOOK-2026-10-19.md cannot be
# re-derived. The 24 fixture .mp4 clips in the same directory are corpus data and stay ignored.
!deployment/artifacts/r48-parity-fixture/
deployment/artifacts/r48-parity-fixture/*
!deployment/artifacts/r48-parity-fixture/*.npz
deployment/features/
figures/*
